<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Etō Shinpei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1834–1874</span> · Also known as Eto Shinpei</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Etō Shinpei was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> of the Saga domain who became a leading statesman of the early Meiji government. As Minister of Justice from 1872 he laid foundations for a modern legal system, but he resigned in 1873 when the government rejected a military expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. In 1874 he led the Saga Rebellion; after its defeat he was captured and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eto-shinpei.jpg" alt="Etō Shinpei" width="320" height="527" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Et%C5%8D_Shinpei.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
